  <sharedRules>
    <rule id="deb1-c539-8fcb-cf61" name="Hammurabic Babylonian (Chariot Wars) - List Notes" publicationId="513c-2d0a-024a-da5a" hidden="false">
      <description>HAMMURABIC BABYLONIAN ARMY LIST (Chariot Wars, pp.19-24).
Characters up to 25% of the army; at least one character to command. A small army of 1,000 points can be commanded by a Senior Officer (or Amorite chief) rather than a General (King, Vassal King or Alik Pani). Chariotry up to 25%. Infantry at least 25%. Allies &amp; Mercenaries up to HALF the points value of the army.
Chariot Runners: up to one unit per unit of Chariotry. Mounted Scouts: the army may not include more mounted scouts than it has characters.

ARMY COMPOSITIONS:
[Hammurabic Babylonian]
  Characters: up to 25%
  Chariotry: up to 25%
  Infantry: at least 25%
  Allies &amp; Mercenaries: up to 50%
  Standard composition.</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
</catalogue>
